      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, there\u0027s no PoC: this isn\u0027t a fix for a known bug. It\u0027s proactive hardening. Each byte-aligned header read now does its own bounds check, with the pointer and remaining size kept together, so the parsing no longer relies on separate length checks staying in step with the reads. That\u0027s the kind of change Patch Rewards covers. Decoded output is unchanged.",
      "parentUuid": "95ea9a9c_894414e8",
      "revId": "c1134e9f9e6a1e094307e0f4d09e11e16cc6dff8",
